<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Alexandros Svolos</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1892–1956</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Alexandros Svolos was a Greek professor of constitutional law who became president of the Political Committee of National Liberation (PEEA), the government set up by the EAM resistance in occupied <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greece">Greece</a>, in April 1944. He then joined the government of national unity of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/georgios-papandreou">Georgios Papandreou</a> and later led small left-wing parties.</p></div>
